-- CK-316: #856 (v1): repeated tuple paths expand to 1,276,786 summary entries, over the 262,144 limit, on a program with no list writes. Expected: checks clean under --ownership-everywhere (v2 does, in 0.03 s).
-- Retain every path's guard without re-expanding identical comparisons.
-- There are no list writes or mutable aliases in this program (#753).
p x = ( x, x )


q x = p (p x)


r x = q (q x)


s x = r (r x)


t x = s (s x)


pub result = t 1 == t 2
